From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winegstreamer: The AVI splitter hands out the streams GStreamer has no caps for (9413)

A 16-bit uncompressed AVI (BI_RGB, or BI_BITFIELDS RGB565) could not be
played: GStreamer's AVI demuxer has no caps for it (video/x-avi-unknown,
no size), decodebin found no decoder and failed the whole file, so the
AVI splitter refused the file and RenderFile returned VFW_E_CANNOT_RENDER.
Windows' AVI splitter hands such a stream out as it is in the file, with
the media type of its own stream header. So does ours now: the splitters
stop autoplugging at an x-avi-unknown stream and take it as it comes, and
the AVI splitter reads the file's strh/strf headers and gives each such
stream the subtype of its bitmap header (RGB1/4/8/555/24/32 by bit count
for BI_RGB, RGB565/555/32 by the BI_BITFIELDS masks, the FOURCC
otherwise, so an installed Video for Windows codec decodes it through
the AVI Decompressor), a VIDEOINFOHEADER carrying that header and the
frame time; audio gets its wave format tag's subtype and WAVEFORMATEX
(an installed ACM codec decodes it). GStreamer turns uncompressed rows
top-down; they are turned back to the file's order.
---
--- a/dlls/winegstreamer/wg_parser.c
+++ b/dlls/winegstreamer/wg_parser.c
@@ -525,8 +525,31 @@
     return parser->no_more_pads;
 }
 
+/* Stained Glass OS (wine-sg 9413): a stream GStreamer's AVI demuxer has no caps for
+ * ("video/x-avi-unknown", "audio/x-avi-unknown": a 16-bit BI_RGB or BI_BITFIELDS
+ * bitmap, a codec only a Video for Windows or ACM driver knows) goes out of the AVI
+ * splitter as it is in the file, as Windows' splitter hands it out: the splitter
+ * gives it the media type of the stream's own format header. decodebin, finding no
+ * decoder for it, failed the whole file before. */
+static bool caps_is_avi_unknown(GstCaps *caps)
+{
+    const char *name;
+
+#ifdef SG_MUTANT_AVI_UNKNOWN_DECODED
+    return false;
+#endif
+    if (!caps || !gst_caps_get_size(caps))
+        return false;
+    name = gst_structure_get_name(gst_caps_get_structure(caps, 0));
+    return !strcmp(name, "video/x-avi-unknown") || !strcmp(name, "audio/x-avi-unknown");
+}
+
 static gboolean autoplug_continue_cb(GstElement * decodebin, GstPad *pad, GstCaps * caps, gpointer user)
 {
+    struct wg_parser *parser = user;
+
+    if (parser->output_compressed && caps_is_avi_unknown(caps))
+        return FALSE;
     return !caps_is_compressed(caps);
 }
 
